        <div class="two-column">
            <div class="column">
                <div class="content-block">
                    <h3 style="font-size: 20px; margin-bottom: 10px;">Human-machine interface</h3>
                    <p>The 615 series relays are equipped with a large graphical display which can show customizable single and multi-line diagrams (SLD) with position indication for the circuit breaker, disconnectors and the earthing switch. Also measured values can be displayed to the chosen standard configuration can be displayed. The SLDs are customized using PC600 and can have multiple pages for easy access to selected information. The data can be accessed not only locally but also via the web browser-based HMI that has now been enriched with a number of usability enhancing features.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="column">
                <div class="content-block">
                    <h3 style="font-size: 20px; margin-bottom: 10px;">The implementation of the IEC 61850 standard covers both vertical and horizontal communication, including GOOSE messaging and parameter setting according to IEC 61850-9-2. The device also supports the IEC 61850-9-2 process bus with sending and receiving of synthetic analog values and sampled values of voltages. In addition to receiving sampled values, the device can be used for synchro-check as well, both in conventional and instrument transformer configurations and also sensor-based applications, to ensure safe interconnection of two networks. For process bus applications, which require high-accuracy time synchronization, IEC 61850-8-1 is supported, and the device supports a redundant Ethernet communication module. In addition, the relays support synchronization over Ethernet using SNTP or over a separate bus using IRIG-B.</h3>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

